{"explanation": "Restrict Caspase inhibition of AKT to mTORC2-OFF context: AKT = (!PTEN & !Caspase) | mTORC2. Unrestricted (!PTEN|mTORC2)&!Caspase forbids any AKT=1 & Caspase=1 coexistence, which removes the apoptosis fixed points that require mTORC2-driven AKT=1 with Caspase=1 (V02,V03,V07,V09). Witnesses retain PTEN=1,mTORC2=0,AKT=0 states, showing AKT-off without Caspase is already expected. Evidence only says p53-induced apoptosis can lead to AKT cleavage, not that it must override mTORC2 activation in all contexts. Conditioning on !mTORC2 keeps Caspase inhibitory (PTEN=0,mTORC2=0: AKT=!Caspase) and preserves PTEN-inhibits and mTORC2-activates influences, while preserving mTORC2-driven apoptosis states. No new regulator invented, only scoping with existing activator.",
  "give_up": false,
  "rule": "(!PTEN & !Caspase) | mTORC2"}
